    "learningObjective": "Master the statutory definitions of Registered Medical Practitioner (RMP), Guardian, and Mentally Ill Person under Section 2.",
    "introduction": "Section 2 provides the technical legal definitions that determine who is authorized to terminate a pregnancy and whose consent is required. Only qualified doctors possessing statutory gynaecological experience can perform terminations.",
    "detailedExplanation": "\n<h3>1. Registered Medical Practitioner (RMP) (Section 2(d))</h3>\n<p>'Registered medical practitioner' means a medical practitioner who possesses any recognized medical qualification as defined in clause (h) of Section 2 of the Indian Medical Council Act, 1956 (now National Medical Commission Act, 2019), whose name has been entered in a State Medical Register and <strong>who has such experience or training in gynaecology and obstetrics as may be prescribed by rules</strong>.</p>\n<p>Under MTP Rules, 2003 (as amended):</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>An RMP must have assisted in at least 25 cases of MTP in an approved hospital; OR</li>\n  <li>Possess a postgraduate degree or diploma in Obstetrics and Gynaecology; OR</li>\n  <li>Have 6 months housemanship in Obstetrics and Gynaecology.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>2. Guardian (Section 2(a))</h3>\n<p>'Guardian' means a person having the care of the person of a <strong>minor or a mentally ill person</strong>. Notice that under the MTP Act, the guardian's consent is relevant ONLY if the pregnant woman is either a minor (under 18 years) or a mentally ill person.</p>\n\n<h3>3. Mentally Ill Person (Section 2(b))</h3>\n<p>Substituted by Act 39 of 2002, 'mentally ill person' means a person who is in need of treatment by reason of any mental disorder <strong>other than mental retardation</strong>. (This aligns with the definition under the Mental Healthcare legislation).</p>\n\n<h3>4. Minor</h3>\n<p>Section 2 does not define minor separately, but under general law and Section 3(4)(a), a minor means a person who has <strong>not attained the age of eighteen (18) years</strong>.</p>\n",
